le lesson  they introduced patterns and  to me that's how i  sort of got a sense of how the language  worked and developed these patterns  which became almost like the frames  around which i could build  my whatever i wanted to say  so uh focus on patterns that's number  three  number four  read a lot  read a lot  and um  when i in my case and and find  interesting things that you want to read  in my case very soon after we um  got past our initial  sound only pinyin only  uh text called chinese dialogues we  graduated to a thing called 20 lectures  on chinese culture 20 lectures on  chinese culture is very interesting  history it consists only of text and a  glossary  no complicated explanations no  no  no  you know quizzes  and and when i look at this and this was  a sort of a lower intermediate book 20  lectures in chinese culture and today i  when i was in china the last time i  bought this you know gauging how you  call you it's advanced spoken chinese  okay it's full of the most  boring  content about so-and-so went to school  and met his friend and they went to the  barber and they went skating and i don't  know what and it's full of questions and  stuff like that and there's only one  thing to do with this kind of book in my  opinion throw it away  i don't like it  unless you're interested in that kind of  stuff so and so when skating  uh  i graduated from 20 lectures in chinese  culture to this reader  in modern chinese which was fascinating  and introduced the patterns and then i  went on to  you know novels like lotus youngza so  read read a lot much easier to do today  because the internet provides so much  content you can use online dictionaries  you can study at link so  read  next  focus on  listening to things that you like in my  case i listened to a lot of xiangsha  but nowadays you can get online you can  go to beijing and buy you can buy  elsewhere cds of the classics of chinese  of history novels you name it loto sions  is available if you look 